cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "DXA Data Extractor"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hoch
    given-names: "Jonathan W."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4992-1199"
    affiliation: "Cardiovascular and Applied Physiology Laboratory, Florida State University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/FSUcaplab/dxa-extractor"
url: "https://github.com/FSUcaplab/dxa-extractor"
license: MIT
date-released: 2026-07-02
abstract: >-
  Desktop GUI tool for batch-extracting body composition and bone density data
  from Hologic DXA PDF summary reports into a single CSV file, built for
  longitudinal research studies with pre/post or multi-timepoint scan designs.
  Auto-detects timepoints and all four Hologic summary report variants,
  corrects the Hologic doubled-character font encoding bug, and extracts
  approximately 96 fields per timepoint including regional fat and lean mass,
  bone mineral content and density, T- and Z-scores, android and gynoid
  regions, and visceral adipose tissue measures.
keywords:
  - dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry
  - DXA
  - body composition
  - bone mineral density
  - visceral adipose tissue
  - PDF data extraction
  - research data management
